== verdict
==============================================================================
  Largest band change with the EOM surface intact to 2.29 A and an absorber from
  2.3 A outward, over all tails, strengths and ramp lengths: 0.02%

  band change against absorber onset (EOM surface intact):
    onset 2.6 A, full strength at 3.0 A:   0.00%
    onset 2.3 A, full strength at 2.7 A:   0.00%
    onset 2.2 A, full strength at 2.6 A:   0.00%
    onset 2.1 A, full strength at 2.5 A:   0.00%
    onset 2.0 A, full strength at 2.4 A:   0.00%
    onset 1.9 A, full strength at 2.3 A:   0.00%
    onset 1.8 A, full strength at 2.2 A:   0.05%
    onset 1.7 A, full strength at 2.1 A:   1.49%
    onset 1.6 A, full strength at 2.0 A:  13.19%
  band change against where the surface is cut (flat beyond):
    V_T flattened beyond 2.10 A:   0.10%
    V_T flattened beyond 1.95 A:   0.73%
    V_T flattened beyond 1.85 A:  11.33%
    V_T flattened beyond 1.78 A:  99.32%

  Positive controls pass: absorber from 1.6 A changes the band 13%,
  flattening beyond 1.78 A changes it 99%. The test can see sensitivity.
  The band starts to respond (>= 1%) to an absorber from 1.7 A and to a surface
  cut at 1.85 A.
  -> The band does not depend on the surface beyond ~2.3 A in this model. CCSD(T) +
     EOM-CCSD out to 2.3 A with an absorber beyond is enough for sigma(lambda, T);
     the 3A'/3A" crossing belongs to product branching.

  Orientation only: 1D peak 373 nm against the measured ~380 nm. Frozen OH and bend,
  Condon, and an absolute sigma sized from 03's f, which is itself uncertain.

